INT. VETERANS HOSPITAL, SLEEP LAB - NIGHT

A dim private room with a single bed and a bank of wires, electrodes, a camera in the ceiling. Through a one-way window: a control room with monitors.

On the bed, wired to the scalp, sleeps SERGEANT MAJOR TIBERIUS NWANKWO-ASHBY (60s, stoic even asleep). At the monitors in the control room sit TECHNICIAN LUCINDA OYELARAN-PARK (30s, clogs, a thermos), DR. WILHELM ACHTERBERG-DIOP (50s, white coat, bow tie), and a student, CALLUM FITZGERALD-ABARA (20s, clipboard).

LUCINDA
Theta waves, stable.

WILHELM
Heart rate?

LUCINDA
Sixty-two.

WILHELM
Good. Callum, note the time.

CALLUM
Three-oh-four.

A speaker on the desk crackles with the patient's breathing, steady.

WILHELM
He should enter REM within the hour.

CALLUM
Doctor, what are we looking for?

WILHELM
Muscle atonia.

CALLUM
I'm sorry?

WILHELM
In REM sleep, the body is paralyzed. Our friend in there--

LUCINDA
Doesn't comply.

WILHELM
He acts out his dreams. Dangerous, for him and anyone near.

CALLUM
What does he dream about?

LUCINDA
We don't ask.

The monitor's line spikes. The speaker emits a low, wet groan.

TIBERIUS (V.O.)
(over speaker, asleep)
Down. Get down.

Lucinda's pen stops. Wilhelm leans forward.

WILHELM
Here we go.

TIBERIUS (V.O.)
(asleep)
Incoming. Down.

On the bed, the old man's arm swings out and strikes the rail. His legs kick the blanket away. The wires pull.

CALLUM
Should we go in?

WILHELM
Not yet.

TIBERIUS (V.O.)
(asleep, hoarse)
Marcus. Marcus, stay down.

Lucinda lowers her head. Wilhelm doesn't move. Callum looks from one to the other and then at his clipboard, where his hand has stopped writing.

TIBERIUS (V.O.)
(asleep)
I've got you. I've got you.

The monitor line smooths. The breathing slows. The arm falls back across the old man's chest.

LUCINDA
(softly)
He's back.

WILHELM
Time?

CALLUM
Three-nineteen.

WILHELM
Record it.

Callum writes, slowly. Lucinda unscrews her thermos and pours coffee into the lid. She holds it out to him without looking.
